# Medication Checker

## Overview

Medication Checker is a web application that allows users to search for medicine information using the OpenFDA Drug Label API. Users simply enter the generic name of a medicine, and the application retrieves important information such as the medicine description, warnings, dosage, and instructions for use.

The application was built using Python, HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. It is deployed on two web servers with HAProxy configured as a load balancer to improve availability and reliability.

---

# Problem Statement

People often need quick access to reliable medicine information before taking medication. Searching through multiple websites can be time-consuming and may lead to inaccurate or incomplete information.

Medication Checker provides a simple solution by allowing users to search for a medicine and retrieve official information directly from the OpenFDA Drug Label API.

---

# Features

- Search medicines by generic name
- View medicine description
- View medicine warnings
- View dosage information
- View instructions for use
- Handles invalid medicine names gracefully
- Responsive user interface
- Deployed on two web servers behind a load balancer

---

