# Running the Application Locally

## Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/medicine-interaction-checker.git
```

## Navigate into the project

```bash
cd medicine-interaction-checker/medication/medication_checker
```

## Install dependencies

```bash
pip install requests
```

## Run the application

```bash
python3 app.py
```

## Open your browser

```
http://localhost:8000
```

---

# Deployment

The application was deployed on three Ubuntu servers.

## Web01

1. Cloned the GitHub repository.
2. Installed the required dependency.

```bash
pip install requests
```

3. Started the application.

```bash
nohup python3 app.py > app.log 2>&1 &
```

4. Configured Nginx as a reverse proxy to forward requests to the Python application running on port 8000.

Example configuration:

```nginx
location / {
    proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;

    proxy_set_header Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
}
```

The following header was also added:

```nginx
add_header X-Served-By $hostname;
```

---

## Web02

The same deployment process used for Web01 was repeated:

- Clone repository
- Install dependencies
- Start the application using `nohup`
- Configure Nginx as a reverse proxy

---

## Load Balancer (Lb01)

HAProxy was configured to distribute incoming requests between Web01 and Web02 using the Round Robin load balancing algorithm.

Example backend configuration:

```haproxy
backend web_back
    balance roundrobin

    server web-01 100.26.186.180:80 check
    server web-02 18.212.74.71:80 check
```

The application was tested by accessing the load balancer to verify that requests were successfully forwarded to both backend web servers.

---

# Deployment Verification

Deployment was verified by:

- Accessing both web servers individually.
- Accessing the application through the load balancer.
- Confirming that the application responded correctly.
- Verifying the `X-Served-By` response header to identify which backend server handled each request.

---

# Challenges Encountered

During the development of this project, I encountered several challenges:

- Understanding the structure of the OpenFDA API responses.
- Some medicines could not be found because they are not available in the OpenFDA database, so I implemented error handling to inform the user when no information is available.
- Running the application in the background so that it continued running after disconnecting from the server.

These challenges were resolved through testing, debugging, and validating each component individually before integrating the entire deployment.

